# Vercel production deploy (secondary)

GitHub Pages is the **primary** host — see `github-pages-deploy.mdc`. After pushing to `main`, also deploy to Vercel **without asking**. Do not wait for “задеплой на Vercel”.

## One project, all products

One Vite app, one Vercel project (`kaik`). A single production deploy updates every product:

| Product | URL path | Source |
|---|---|---|
| Site (course) | `/` | `index.html` |
| Admin | `/admin` | `admin.html` |
| Catalog | `/catalog` | `catalog.html` |

Do not treat them as separate apps. Do not skip a deploy because “only admin changed”.

Live host: `https://kaik-one.vercel.app`

## How to ship

There is often **no git repo**. Prefer CLI deploy of the working tree:

```bash
NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0 vercel deploy --prod --yes --project kaik --logs
```

- `--prod` is required (not a preview URL).
- Always `git push origin main` first (GitHub Pages). Vercel CLI is the secondary step after that push.
- Do not update git config. Do not commit secrets (`.env`, tokens).
- If TLS intercept blocks the CLI, keep `NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0` for that command only.

## After deploy

Reply with the three live URLs:

- https://kaik-one.vercel.app/
- https://kaik-one.vercel.app/admin
- https://kaik-one.vercel.app/catalog
